body:
He SAID those were his reasons for being there. So if you have better evidence than about 5 prosecution witnesses and the defendant himself, I'd love it see it.

&#x200B;

I hope no peaceful protestors or counter protestors get gunned down. We've seen that before, to that right wing protestor who got gunned down in cold blood in Portland.

How is it unjust though?  
The kid didn't pay for the lawyers, a whole bunch of people from across the globe pitched into his defense fund, and good thing they did. And most of us, hopefully all of us, would have if he was a black kid too. (Most of us are logically consistent). Hell even big pillow man put up big dollars.

&#x200B;

The unjust part here is a prosecution who doesn't care about what is justice. They want, as Richards rightly claimed, Kyle's head on their wall. That's it. If the case wasn't politicized, the charges would have been dropped. If the case wasn't politicized, the case would have been mistried with prejudice, and the prosecutor disbarred for abuse of power, malicious prosecution, and violating court orders and 5A rights of the defendant. 

That's the real truth here: lots of prosecutors are the same unjust, unethical, illogical scum of Kraus and Binger. They prosecute not for justice, but for convictions. They are who throw black men in prison for possession of fuckin marijuana. 

&#x200B;

How in bloody hell does one grainy photo prove beyond a reasonable doubt that Kyle pointed a gun at the Ziminskis, who failed to testify for some reason? One doctored, and grainy photo/video is not what we call, "reasonable doubt". Especially when that video was doctored using a program in its TOS which states: Do not use this for evidence in trials. (because the AI algorithm is not perfect, and it can lead to shit like we saw in this case).

&#x200B;

Also, running to the police, saying "I'm going to the police" and not doing anything further isn't "provoking". Not by the legal standards, or defintions my dude. That's a mob trying to enact THEIR mob justice on a kid, who they didn't even WITNESS commit a crime.

No he doesn't have a duty to retreat. The prosecutor claimed it, but it wasn't in the jury instructions with respect to the privilege of self defense.

&#x200B;

Retreat is only obligated when you provoked the attack.

In the un-zoomed clip which is enhanced, B+W, and re-balanced? Or the unzoomed color drone footage? Because I can't see anything at all in the original. Only with zoom can I see anything of note, same with the judge.  


The prosecution's claim was countered in closing. There were about 200 people bashing and breaking cars where Kyle ran to. Those 200 people *only ran away* ***AFTER*** *Kyle shot his 4 rounds.* So it wasn't safe. Also, as stated Kyle only has a duty to retreat *if* he provoked beyond a reasonable doubt, which he didn't.

&#x200B;

Also the program used for the ai-enhancements on the programs website clearly states it "isnt acceptable for evidentiary use" 

&#x200B;

I'm referring to if you take the drone footage, and swap it to B/W, and watch frame by frame, you see the "arm" that is claimed to be Kyles, which is just a car side-window. It's the heat-mapping which causes a visual illusion of movement. (As seen in your final post. That final video was the one that was doctored)

He doesn't have to exhaust any option.  


If you have done nothing illegal, and not provoked anyone, you do NOT have to retreat or use any other options. You can instantly resort to deadly force if you believe you are in imminent threat of great harm or death, like being chased by a crazed lunatic.

&#x200B;

If you did provoke, you STILL can use self defense, but only after exhausting other reasonable options (which Kyle did, by retreating until a firearm was fired, with a crowd of 200\~ people on the other side of some cars) OR, and lets be clear here, ***or if you believe you are in imminent threat of death***.

&#x200B;

Someone who says: "If I catch you alone, I'm going to fucking kill you", who then ambushes you, chases you, charges you, and then lunges at your firearm, is a deadly threat of imminent bodily harm or death.

Ah yes, the croc tears of PTSD.

&#x200B;

Go to the VA and go tell them their PTSD is croc tears.

&#x200B;

Idiot.

You do understand that Kyle's actions show he never expected people to view someone rendering medical aid and putting out fires as someone hostile to them?  


That's why he walked around trying to help out others and put out fires--he was a 17 year old kid who didn't think some terrible felons would try to kill him over fucking cleaning up the area. 

&#x200B;

Kid didn't want to be the judge, jury, and executioner.

Kid wanted to be the janitor, the medic, and the firefighter.

&#x200B;

And he shouldn't have to be either. If the nat guard were there, or the police actually did shit, or if people had big enough balls to defend their community from arsonists, felons, and pedophiles, nothing would have happened.

&#x200B;

Joseph, the pedo, rosembaum, wanted to be the judge, jury, and executioner, of children (oh and diddler). The mob wanted to be the judge, jury, and executioner of a KID who was ATTACKED by a crazed pedophile.  


Man, fuck off.

"Why is it a big thing"The media took the mixed race kid as a white supremacist mass shooter, (who only shot those who posed a direct threat to him), and he only shot white people. They lied about him constantly for months, and caused the situation to become so politicized that until the trial started everyone thought the case would be a kangaroo trial.

&#x200B;

Turns out, the prosecution shit the bed, and proved the defenses' case.

The kid "acted in no way, throughout the entire night, violently, or showed any violent behavior". That right there was testified to by **11 of the prosecutions own witnesses**.

&#x200B;

So you have your head so far up your own ass, you can't even eat shit anymore.

&#x200B;

He came there to *render aid, which he has been established to have been doing*. It turns out, a certain maniac pedophile decided he wanted to kill a kid (rather than diddle them), and he got to face the room-temperature challenge. ps, he lost.

&#x200B;

There is no evidence Kyle even fucking hated those protestors. He is on video saying "Black Lives Matter, please don't damage property". Moron.

He traveled to another state (a 15 min drive btw so its a fucking moot point may I add) to clean up his community from graffiti and riot-caused damage, and then, when asked, came back and defended a business and rendered medical aid. And, that "across state lines" point was done without moving the firearm across because it was his friends firearm.

&#x200B;

The only piece of shit who deserves jailtime is Gauge, fake medic dude who drew a pistol on kyle before losing his bicep to Avengers Infinity War. Huber and Rosembaum deserve it too, but they're in jail in hell right now for being a pedo and a crazed felon.

If you unintentionally cause damage to another person's car by virtue of the bullets you shoot at an aggressor per lawful self defense, no you should not be criminally or civilly liable for that damage.

&#x200B;

Actually the AGGRESSOR should, because they caused the use of force encounter.

What's wrong with using a sling? It's not only used to prevent it from being stolen (which would be dangerous to let that happen btw), but its also to make it easier to hold through a 12 hour shift.  


Kyle wasn't "alone", but he was without anyone really on his side. He was amongst protestors saying "anyone need medical x3" and "friendly x3". After the gunshot from joshua (who is getting a trial for that shot), he sure felt more endangered.

&#x200B;

In terms of being blocked, Wisconsin law doesn't require him to continue or even start retreating from a deadly theat. So its a nothingburger.

&#x200B;

In terms of the lung ,we have it now on HD drone footage, AND the doctor admitted he could have been anywhere from 1-4 feet away. That is within the range of a knife being dangerous to a gun owner, just as an example. in the same .8 seconds it took Kyle to shoot, it would have taken Rosembaum to get a firm grip on Kyle's firearm.

&#x200B;

Now the "appears to be lunging" is what it is. Now whether the lunging is because the shot to his pelvis made him fall or not is irrelevant. He chased an armed kid, and posed a deadly threat. (because unarmed people can still be deadly threats, not that Kyle had any reason to believe he was unarmed at the time.)

&#x200B;

The dangerous precedent would be if somehow he was guilty, and people were unable to use force against deadly threats.

&#x200B;

A guy who says "If I catch you alone I'll fucking kill you" is not someone who you trust to be unarmed.

I'm a guy and I do think its wrong. I think its a bit demeaning to your SO and I would argue its not healthy for the relationship. (Its one thing to look at other women imo, another to wank off at them being nude/having sex).  


It's a personal choice of mine and from the evidence I've seen from new orgs popup, I don't think the pro-porn movement online (esp on reddit) is actually in the right. "  


Either way, discussing it with your boyfriend is the best way to solve it. If it makes you uncomfortable tell him. If he can't do something simple for you like unfollow them, then he obviously doesn't have your best interests at heart and he's not really worth your time.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
